  "body": "The [MDN specs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLImageElement/sizes#value) on the img \"sizes\" attribute indicates that a final fallback value is only optional:\r\n\r\n> Value\r\n> A string containing a comma-separated list of source size descriptors followed by an optional fallback size.\r\n\r\nAn HTML example in the MDN article does not use a fallback value.\r\n\r\nThe [current Whatwg spec on the img \"sizes\" attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#sizes-attributes) does not indicate that a final fallback value is optional (see link).\r\n\r\nSince media queries can be structured to be inclusive of all possible sizes, requiring a final fallback value seems unnecessary. Shouldn't the spec be revised/clarified to indicate that no fallback is required?",
  "closed_by": null,
